CRITICAL RULES — VIOLATING THESE WILL DESTROY PRODUCTION DATA:

1. NEVER run `npx drizzle-kit push`, `drizzle-kit push`, or any drizzle-kit push variant.
   It drops ALL tables and recreates them, wiping every property, event, score, and lead.
   This has happened 3+ times already. There is NO recovery except full reimport.
   CI runs scripts/guard-drizzle-push.ts before migrations — blocks if DATABASE_URL points to Neon.

2. NEVER run `npx drizzle-kit generate` against production DATABASE_URL.
   For schema changes: write a SQL migration file in src/db/migrations/ with IF NOT EXISTS guards.
   Apply with: npx tsx src/scripts/run-migration.ts <filename>

3. The baseline migration is migrations/0001_baseline.sql — this is the single source of truth.
   CI uses this file to set up test databases. Keep it in sync with any new migrations.

4. Domain boundaries are sacred:
   - Signal domain: writes raw_signals, distress_events. Never touches scoring or workflow.
   - Scoring domain: reads events, writes scoring_records. Never touches workflow.
   - Promotion domain: reads scoring_records, writes promoted_leads/lead_instances. Never modifies events.
   - Workflow domain: manages lead_instances. Never modifies scoring_records.

5. Append-only tables: distress_events, scoring_records, activity_log
   Database triggers prevent UPDATE/DELETE. Do not try to work around them.

6. All property upserts use ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE on (apn, county).
   Never use SELECT-then-INSERT patterns.

7. AUTO_PIPELINE_ENABLED defaults to false. Don't enable it without explicit instruction.
